# Alexandria and Documentation

## Alexandria (`alexandria/`)

Crate `lovelace_alexandria` in `alexandria/` is a **static** library. It owns:

- Parsing Lovelace **comments** and **doc-comments** (format TBC)
- Building a documentation model from a project, solution, or package
- Generating **Markdown** (`.md`) output, with **SVG** diagrams when they clarify structure (modules, deps, types)

`lovelace doc` is a thin CLI over Alexandria. Do not generate docs in `compiler/` or `lovelace/` besides calling this library.

## `lovelace doc`

Produces a Markdown documentation set for the selected project, solution, or Hypatia package. Graphs are SVG files referenced from the Markdown when needed.

## Embed docs in artifacts

Documentation from doc-comments may also be **embedded as attributes** in generated **WASM**, **WAT**, and **WIT** (WIT `///` docs and/or custom sections / annotations). The compiler backend emits this; Alexandria supplies the text/model. Do not drop docs on the floor at codegen time.

## Host Ada API docs (GNATdoc)

Host Ada specs are annotated for [GNATdoc 4](https://docs.adacore.com/live/wave/gnatdoc4/html/gnatdoc-doc/annotations.html) (`--style=leading`). This is **not** Alexandria (`lovelace doc`). Run `scripts/gnatdoc.ps1` after `alr` has generated crate `config/` GPRs. See gnatdoc and [docs/gnatdoc.md](docs/gnatdoc.md).

## `docs/` (this repository)

When a **new feature is implemented**, document it under `docs/` in the same effort (not a later leftover).

`docs/` must grow to include, as those features exist:

- How to use the **`lovelace` CLI** (every command and flag)
- The Lovelace **language grammar**
- **HOW TOs**, e.g. how to create a native/WASI binding for Lovelace, how to author a Hypatia package

## Lovelace source docs

Every subroutine **visible outside its Lovelace module** must have a doc-comment. Undocumented public API is a compile-time defect once doc-comments are implemented (warning, subject to Lovelace Werror).